opened in time for the World Cup this  new part of Hamad International Airport  has been designed to offer often tired  and stressed out passengers a different  travel experience  the vision is to completely change the  idea of  in the aviation industry for passengers  who are used to come in narrow corridors  dark places where stressed the time they  step their foot into the airport until  they get into their their Ploy this is  what we wanted to change  the main Concourse contains a 6 000  square meter tropical garden it's made  up of 300 trees and 25 000 plants  sourced from sustainable forests in  Malaysia and Thailand in order for the  rainforest to thrive indoors this  building has been designed in a  particular way for example the roof  above me is made out of special glass  which controls and filters the light  surrounding the tropical garden are 65  new shops and restaurants  the main terminal has been expanded by  125 000 square meters and passenger  capacity has increased by nearly 50  percent it's quite significant because  it is raising the capacity of Hamad  International from 40 million to 58  million passengers of course this is not  the ultimate capacity we aim for Hamad  International but we are getting there  very close to what eventual capacity of  over 70 million passengers we envisage  with the final expansion that will start  taking place soon after FIFA  the first passage is to use this part of  the terminal will depart on a flight  from Doha to Kuwait on Friday there are  five new gates in this area airport  authorities say the number of arrivals  and departures from here will increase  steadily in the coming days Victoria  Gayton B Al Jazeera Doha
 

